@startuml
!theme toy
title GPU passes in one frame: submission order on the graphics queue

start
:WorldLight.SourceUpload\n1 dispatch per pending chunk,\nthen matter clear/scatter/finalize,\nthen occupancy rebuild; <<#FFB347>>
:WorldLight.RadianceAtlas\ncompute gather; <<#FFB347>>
:WorldLight.FieldUpdate\nfield copy · dirty cascades · ordinary cascades; <<#FFB347>>
note right
  All three need initialized field lighting.
  SourceUpload also needs a pending source update.
end note

:Grid.Backdrop render pass\noffscreen RGBA16F · fullscreen background; <<#CF9FFF>>
note right
  Skipped without a world background,
  and when MSAA draws the background directly.
end note

:Grid.Visibility phase 0\nreset indirect args · 1 workgroup; <<#FFB347>>
:Grid.Visibility phase 1\nfrustum cull · N workgroups; <<#FFB347>>
note right : global barrier after each phase

:Particles.Pack; <<#FFB347>>
:Particles.Cull; <<#FFB347>>
:Particles.CullPrefix · 1 workgroup; <<#FFB347>>
:Particles.CullCompact; <<#FFB347>>
:Liquids.Elements render pass\noffscreen; <<#CF9FFF>>
:Liquids.Thickness render pass\noffscreen; <<#CF9FFF>>
:Liquids.Filter compute; <<#FFB347>>
:Solids.Elements render pass\noffscreen; <<#CF9FFF>>
:Solids.Coverage render pass\noffscreen; <<#CF9FFF>>
note right
  The particle chain needs GPU particles.
  Pack also needs changed source, terrain or metadata.
  Liquid and solid passes need the matching material.
end note

:scene render pass begins\ntarget: surface (native)\nor retro scene target (offscreen); <<#CF9FFF>>
:background fullscreen draw; <<#CF9FFF>>
:terrain opaque indirect draw; <<#CF9FFF>>
:Particles.Draw\nLiquids.Composite · Solids.Composite · particle disk; <<#CF9FFF>>
:terrain translucent indirect draw\noptical-blend material only; <<#CF9FFF>>
:TrianglePass draws; <<#CF9FFF>>
:scene render pass ends; <<#CF9FFF>>

if (offscreen presentation?) then (yes)
  :Spatial resolve compute\nspatial or temporal2x; <<#B0B0B0>>
  :Temporal resolve render pass\ntemporal, not spatial or 2x; <<#B0B0B0>>
  :Temporal2x resolve compute\nwhen enabled; <<#B0B0B0>>
  :Auto exposure\nhistogram then exposure compute\nwhen enabled; <<#B0B0B0>>
  :Bloom compute\nwhen enabled; <<#B0B0B0>>
  :RetroPass::render\nfullscreen composite in the surface scene pass; <<#CF9FFF>>
else (no)
endif

:UI render pass\nsurface · LoadOp::Load; <<#CF9FFF>>
:ui.detached draws; <<#CF9FFF>>
:submit command buffer → fence V; <<#B0B0B0>>
:queue present; <<#B0B0B0>>

stop

legend right
  orange = compute pass · purple = render pass
  grey = offscreen branch or submit/present boundary
  Rows are pass boundaries; rows between the scene pass begin/end are its draws.
  A pass may contain several dispatches.
  Offscreen is requested by retro, palette, HDR, temporal or native samples;
  the native path skips that branch.
  One graphics queue: encode order is execution order.
endlegend
@enduml
